  General methodology: The global approach considered in this     7825 1451
          work is presented in the following paper: Modern        7825 1451
          nuclear data evaluation with the TALYS code system,     7825 1451
          A.J. Koning and D. Rochman, Nuclear Data Sheets 113     7825 1451
          (2012) 2841.                                            7825 1451
                                                                  7825 1451
  MF2:  Resolved resonance range  (RRR)                           7825 1451
       The RRR was generated with TARES-1.31, compiled on         7825 1451
       12-10-2015 11:58:11 PM at Villingen  , Switzerland. The RRR7825 1451
       expands from 0 to 1.076040E+3 eV. A total of               7825 1451
       2 l-values are used and 66 resonances. The resonance       7825 1451
       formalism is multi-level Breit Wigner (MLBW).              7825 1451
       The ladder approach from the CALENDF code is used to       7825 1451
       generate statistical resonances in the unresolved          7825 1451
       resonance range. Therefore, the URR is translated into     7825 1451
       resolved resonance range. Explanations about the method    7825 1451
       can be found in the CALENDF manual: CEA-Report CEA-R-6277  7825 1451
       "CALENDF-2010: User manual" by J.C. Sublet, P. Ribon and   7825 1451
       M. Coste-Delcaux.                                          7825 1451
       The method of creating statistical resonances in the       7825 1451
       URR region is described in: "From average parameters to    7825 1451
       statistical resolved resonances", D. Rochman et al.,       7825 1451
       Annals of Nucl. Ene. 51 (2013) 60.                         7825 1451
       The s-wave average level spacing is 22.85 eV and           7825 1451
       the s-wave neutron strength is 0.0001486 1e-4.             7825 1451
